  "body": "First cut of #688: the documentation site, built with Zola and published to GitHub Pages from the tag-triggered release workflow. The browser build (`/app/`) waits for #31; the front page says it is coming.\n\n## What changed\n- **`site/`** - a Zola project with our own Tera templates (`base`, `index`, `section`, `page`) and one plain stylesheet: no third-party theme, no framework, no JavaScript. Light/dark follows the OS.\n  - **User guide** (`content/guide/`): Install, First run, Setups, Operations, Posting, Reading a refusal.\n  - **Developers** (`content/developers/`): Crate map, Commands and undo, Test gates (`cargo xtask gate`), Releases.\n  - Front page: what CamCraft is, the pre-1.0 caution, the version the site was built from with a download link to that release, and the \"browser build is coming (#31)\" note.\n  - Written from the README, AGENTS.md, RELEASE_NOTES.md, `docs/MACHINE-ONBOARDING.md` and the code (ribbon labels, tab names, `KindInfo::ALL` captions, `posting.rs` refusal messages, the Post refused window). Clean room: only CamCraft's own behaviour; no vendor text, no Fusion output.\n- **`.github/workflows/release.yml`** - **needs the maintainer's look** (`.github` change):\n  - `site` job (contents: read): installs Zola **v0.23.6** (musl binary from the official release, SHA-256 checked), reads `[workspace.package] version`, refuses a tag that doesn't name it, writes `site/version.toml`, runs `zola build --base-url https://<owner>.github.io/<repo>`, uploads with `actions/upload-pages-artifact@v5`. On a manual dispatch it only builds.\n  - `pages` job: `actions/deploy-pages@v5`, `pages: write` + `id-token: write` scoped to this job only, `github-pages` environment, `pages` concurrency group. Runs only on a tag, when `site` and `publish` both succeeded, so the site's download link never points at a missing release.\n  - **No new trigger**; the workflow default stays `contents: read`.\n- `.gitignore`: `site/public/`, `site/version.toml`. Nothing generated is committed.\n- `docs/decisions/688-docs-site.md`: the choices and what was dropped.\n\n## Repo settings the deploy needs (cannot be set from a workflow)\n- Settings > Pages > Source: **GitHub Actions**.\n- Environment `github-pages` > deployment branches and tags: allow tags `v*.*.0` (the default allows protected branches only and would refuse a tag deploy).\n\n## How tested\nZola 0.23.6 (official aarch64-apple-darwin binary, checksum-verified, in a temp dir):\n- `zola build` -> `Creating 10 pages (0 orphan) and 2 sections`, no warnings.\n- `zola check` -> `Site content: 10 pages (0 orphan), 2 sections`, every internal and external link OK (one GitHub `#anchor` link that Zola can't resolve was dropped).\n- With `version.toml` = 0.16.0 and `--base-url https://mkinney.github.io/Camcraft`: front page reads \"This site documents CamCraft 0.16.0\" with a link to `releases/tag/v0.16.0`, footer \"Built from CamCraft 0.16.0\", all asset and page links carry the base path; without the file it says it's a local preview.\n- The workflow's version `sed` run locally against `Cargo.toml` -> `0.16.0`; the musl tarball's checksum and layout (`zola` at the root) checked; the YAML parses (jobs: ..., publish, site, pages).\n- No Rust changed, so no cargo gate applies.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The Pages deploy itself: it runs only on a pushed `vX.Y.0` tag. The `site` job's Linux steps ran only as their local equivalents above.\n- Actions minutes: the first tag run's added minutes get measured and reported on #688 afterwards (the `site` job is a ~10 MB download plus a sub-second build; `pages` is a deploy).\n- AGENTS.md's release steps don't name the site step yet: that's a process-file change (PROCESS_VERSION bump, #681 note), left for a process PR once the job has run once.\n\nChangelog: Documentation site (user guide and developer docs) built with Zola and published to GitHub Pages at each release tag (#688)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nfork synced at v0.16.0\n\nRefs #688\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
